   "notes": "Cambridge University Press Bookshop (no.28): weathered gault brick, 4 bays (2+2 either side of a downpipe) x 2 floors of 6/6 sashes with white keystone lintels, white band/parapet, slate mansard with 4 dormers (modelled as windows in the skin above the cornice). Stuccoed ground floor: red panelled door with fanlight at W end, two arched-transom shop windows, central entrance, further window at E end; fascia is blank stucco ('28'). Near-frontal 2022-23 photo. Walls :1-:4 not verified."
